        "abstract": "The authors discuss the use of mode-locked solid state and dye lasers as the optical sources. Such lasers are capable of generating a continuous measurement bandwidth of thousands of gigahertz at a variety of wavelengths. Two measurements are discussed: direct microwave based detection and opto-electronic sampling. The devices tested and used as examples include an indium tin oxide (ITO)-GaAs Schottky photodiode and GaInAs PIN photodiode with bandwidths of 110 GHz and 25 GHz respectively.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
